WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:04.850
Figuring out what to watch on Netflix can
take about as long as actually watching whatever

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.359
movie you decide on.

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.030
Life doesn't need to be that hard, so we've
collected a list of the best movies you can

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:13.660
watch on Netflix right now, no aimless browsing
required.

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.630
From incredible underrated gems to timeless
favorites that you haven't thought about in

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:22.220
years, we've rounded up the best movies on
Netflix right now.

00:00:22.220 --> 00:00:24.220
Kubo and the Two Strings

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:29.800
From the studio behind Coraline and ParaNorman,
Kubo and the Two Strings marks yet another

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.910
visually stunning achievement in stop-motion
animation.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:38.440
The story follows Kubo, a young street performer
in feudal Japan who uses his two-string guitar

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:40.710
to make origami come to life.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:45.560
Little does he know that he's the focal point
of a supernatural war raging unseen all around

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:46.560
him.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:50.719
Kubo and the Two Strings is an epic adventure
that's billed as a kids' movie but probably

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:53.440
holds even more magic for the adults in the
room.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.000
(laughs)

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.080
"The mighty beetle is victorious!"

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.260
(screams in fear)

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.960
The Imitation Game

00:01:02.969 --> 00:01:08.550
Helmed by Passengers director Morten Tyldum,
The Imitation Game is an Oscar-winning look

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:13.660
into the tumultuous life of Alan Turing, the
mathematician largely responsible for breaking

00:01:13.660 --> 00:01:16.070
the Enigma code during World War II.

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:20.380
Benedict Cumberbatch delivers an incredible
performance as Turing, turning a potentially

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:26.000
dry historical period piece into an emotional
journey charged with high-tension drama.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.360
He's backed up by an equally convincing Keira
Knightley, who offsets Cumberbatch's cold,

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:34.060
off-putting genius with genuine warmth.

00:01:34.060 --> 00:01:37.280
Both were nominated for Oscars that year,
and for good reason.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:41.610
The Imitation Game is definitely a movie everyone
should see at least once.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:44.880
"Miss Clarke, did you really solve this puzzle
yourself?"

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:49.340
"What makes you think I couldn't solve this
by myself?"

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:52.380
The Babadook

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:56.880
The Babadook focuses on an exhausted single
mother finding it harder and harder to love

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.530
her weird kid, who's just a bit mentally unstable.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.140
It's a horrifying premise even before the
monster arrives.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.950
The movie itself is pure horror, far removed
from the typical grab bag of jump scares and

00:02:08.950 --> 00:02:12.200
loud, jarring audio cues you find in most
horror movies.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:16.850
But it's also touching, heartwarming, and
impossibly human in its emotions.

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:22.020
Put simply, The Babadook is so far removed
from cliché that it'll probably start a few

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:23.720
new clichés of its own.

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:28.440
"If it's in a word or in a look, you can't
get rid of the babadook."

00:02:29.800 --> 00:02:30.800
Oldboy

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:38.370
Gritty, moving, gut-wrenching, and beautiful,
2003's Oldboy succeeded on two levels: one,

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:41.750
it breathed new life into the hard-boiled
revenge genre.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:45.950
Two, it brought Korean films into the international
spotlight.

00:02:45.950 --> 00:02:51.320
Oldboy tells the story of Oh Dae-Su, a middle-aged
drunk who is kidnapped and locked in a room

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:53.090
for 15 years.

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:58.660
When he's inexplicably released one day, Oh
Dae-Su embarks on an emotional, blood-soaked

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.930
journey of revenge against the man who imprisoned
him.

00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:06.730
What follows is a violent, touching story
of regrets and revenge with one of the most

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:10.450
impressive action scenes ever put to film.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:11.530
Beasts Of No Nation

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:18.550
Netflix's first original feature film, Beasts
of No Nation stars Idris Elba as a ruthless

00:03:18.550 --> 00:03:23.940
commander and newcomer Abraham Attah as a
boy soldier named Agu.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:28.990
Beasts of No Nation is powerful, shockingly
real, and heartbreaking in its portrayal of

00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:31.170
the unspeakable horrors of war.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:36.000
It's not an easy film to watch, the pace is
relentless, the imagery is visceral, but it's

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.440
also undeniably a movie worth your time.

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:40.610
The Fundamentals of Caring

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.950
Heartwarming, poignant, and injected with
more lewd jokes and profanity than a Farrelly

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:51.209
Brothers comedy, The Fundamentals of Caring
is still an incredibly human and real experience.

00:03:51.209 --> 00:03:56.180
The movie follows Paul Rudd as a newly certified
caregiver working with his first patient,

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:58.420
a wisecracking teenage shut-in.

00:03:58.420 --> 00:04:03.880
After a rocky start, they set out on a road
trip to see a series of roadside attractions,

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:08.620
and along the way they both learn valuable
lessons about family and friendship without

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:10.190
ever getting really sappy.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:14.900
"The bad news is that she's refusing to sing
'Fireworks.'

00:04:16.920 --> 00:04:20.180
Apparently, she's done that with the last
four make-a-wish kids."

00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.120
Captain America: Civil War

00:04:23.130 --> 00:04:29.280
Undeniably the biggest installment in the
MCU since The Avengers, 2016's Captain America:

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:33.870
Civil War is proof that Marvel finally figured
out how to nail a sequel.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.370
It's a tour de force of high-stakes action
mixed with character-driven drama and all

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:39.970
the right dashes of humor.

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:44.310
Even beyond that, the movie reckons with the
troubling idea that there are consequences

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:47.320
to all the mayhem and destruction we love
to watch on screen.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:48.940
"Give me a break!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:52.240
I'm doing what has to be done.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:54.740
To stave off something worse."

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:58.740
The Wailing

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:04.470
Equal parts drama, psychological horror, and
supernatural thriller, The Wailing never stops

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:06.470
to take a breath once it gets rolling.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:12.090
In a quiet South Korean village, a mysterious
disease leads to an outbreak of violent behavior

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:13.400
among the residents.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.750
When his daughter starts showing symptoms,
a bumbling police officer digs deeper into

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:22.720
the plague and stumbles into a battle between
good and evil that threatens to tear the village

00:05:22.720 --> 00:05:23.960
to pieces.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:29.040
Beautifully shot, terrifying at times, and
scientific proof that Korean exorcisms are

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:34.380
way cooler than ours, The Wailing should be
on every horror fan's watch list.

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.080
Gangs of New York

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:42.480
Martin Scorsese is a master at capturing the
world of gangsters in any time period.

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:47.310
Few films showcase that gift better than Gangs
of New York, which sees the clash of street

00:05:47.310 --> 00:05:51.730
gangs in 19th-century New York City reach
gritty new heights.

00:05:51.730 --> 00:05:56.540
Gangs of New York is one of the director's
many examples of near-perfect storytelling,

00:05:56.540 --> 00:06:00.540
with beautiful cinematography, a sweeping
narrative, and pitch-perfect performances

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.460
from every actor involved.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:06.900
This is not only one of the best movies on
Netflix, but one of the best movies, period.

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:09.020
"Well then, we got business."

00:06:10.440 --> 00:06:11.860
"That we do."

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:18.830
It Follows

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:24.260
"No clichés, no disappointments" must have
been the mantra of writer/director David Robert

00:06:24.260 --> 00:06:28.120
Mitchell when he set out to put It Follows
on the big screen.

00:06:28.120 --> 00:06:33.020
The movie follows a simple premise, but sticks
with it the whole way and, makes an effort

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:37.139
to only let the premium chills make it past
the cutting-room floor.

00:06:37.139 --> 00:06:41.190
The story follows a young woman who finds
that she's been saddled with a curse after

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:43.220
sleeping with her new boyfriend.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:46.199
Something is coming for her, something slow
but persistent.

00:06:46.199 --> 00:06:49.520
The only way to pass the curse on is to sleep
with someone else.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.420
It Follows comes in strong with a strong timeless
aesthetic and keeps you guessing until the

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:55.760
end.

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:57.540
The Hateful Eight

00:06:57.540 --> 00:07:02.930
In the aftermath of the Civil War, eight people
get snowed in at a roadside pit-stop, and

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.800
as the title asserts, none of them are particularly
savory characters.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:11.630
There's a lot of talking, a lot of bloodshed,
and a lot of Tarantino-ness all around.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:16.090
The Hateful Eight might not be Tarantino's
best film, but it's definitely one of his

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:20.699
most interesting, with a haunting setup that
resembles a horror movie more than the Western

00:07:20.699 --> 00:07:21.970
setting it takes place in.

00:07:21.970 --> 00:07:28.699
"You come back with anything but a guitar,
my pistol plays a tune.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:31.100
'Domergue's Death March.'

00:07:31.100 --> 00:07:32.740
You got it?"

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:35.240
The Fellowship of the Ring

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.990
Even after 17 years, The Fellowship of the
Ring feels like a blockbuster that could have

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:40.990
been made yesterday.

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:46.289
The sweeping intro to Peter Jackson's epic
trilogy was overshadowed by its sequels, so

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:49.669
it's easy to forget how incredible the first
one was.

00:07:49.669 --> 00:07:55.300
The Mines of Moria, the Balrog, Gandalf escaping
from Isengard on an eagle...

00:07:55.300 --> 00:07:57.639
The movie is packed to the brim with perfect
scenes.

00:07:57.639 --> 00:08:02.600
Heck, the intro monologue alone is usually
enough to convince anyone to watch the film.

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:07.050
"It began with the forging of the great rings.

00:08:07.050 --> 00:08:08.889
Three were given to the elves.

00:08:08.889 --> 00:08:13.340
Immortal, fairest, and wisest of all beings."

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:14.580
The Godfather

00:08:14.580 --> 00:08:19.410
Time and time again, The Godfather has been
rated as one of the best movies of all time.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:24.460
The story needs little introduction, Vito
Corleone, played by Marlon Brando, is retiring

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:29.710
as the head of the infamous Corleone crime
family; and his mantle of mafia Don gets passed

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:33.060
down to his reluctant son, Michael, played
by Al Pacino.

00:08:33.060 --> 00:08:37.559
These characters may exist in a violent world
most of us have never experienced, but they

00:08:37.559 --> 00:08:39.789
feel as real as your next door neighbors.

00:08:39.789 --> 00:08:44.100
A lot of people toss around the word "masterpiece"
when they're talking about movies, but The

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:48.970
Godfather is one of the few films that truly
deserves the honor.

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:50.410
Wind River

00:08:50.410 --> 00:08:54.959
When a girl is found murdered on a Native
American reserve in Wyoming, the discovery

00:08:54.959 --> 00:08:59.850
launches a harrowing investigation led by
Cory Lambert, an expert tracker with his own

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.209
dark past.

00:09:01.209 --> 00:09:05.089
It's tempting to say that Jeremy Renner's
performance as Lambert is the highlight of

00:09:05.089 --> 00:09:09.959
Wind River, but the movie is so deftly woven
together that there's no one standout.

00:09:09.959 --> 00:09:14.850
From the gorgeous, icy landscape shots to
the heart-pounding pace, Wind River is just

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:17.389
an all-around incredible movie.

00:09:17.389 --> 00:09:18.699
Changeling

00:09:18.699 --> 00:09:24.720
Angelina Jolie stars as Christine Collins,
a woman whose son goes missing for five months

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:26.970
before the police find him and bring him home.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:28.310
Happy ending, right?

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:29.369
Not quite.

00:09:29.369 --> 00:09:34.529
Convinced that the boy returned to her isn't
her son, Collins fights back against the LAPD,

00:09:34.529 --> 00:09:37.870
who in turn respond by labeling her insane.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:42.449
Jolie's performance in Changeling is near
flawless as a mother on the brink of losing

00:09:42.449 --> 00:09:46.730
her sanity, and director Clint Eastwood is
in top form from beginning to end.

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:51.860
More than anything, Changeling completely
immerses you in the world of 1920s America,

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:56.350
albeit a more paranoid, thrilling version
of 1920s America than you're likely to find

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:58.769
in the history books.

00:09:58.769 --> 00:10:00.300
City of God

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:05.489
Visually striking and punishingly brutal,
City of God follows several children in the

00:10:05.489 --> 00:10:10.389
slums of Rio de Janeiro, Brazil, as they grow
up surrounded by gang violence.

00:10:10.389 --> 00:10:14.560
As soon as they're old enough to hold a gun,
they leave their childhood behind and cross

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:18.779
the divide into executions, robberies, and
drugs.

00:10:18.779 --> 00:10:22.929
Director Fernando Meirelles went on to helm
the Oscar-winning The Constant Gardener just

00:10:22.929 --> 00:10:27.519
a few years after City of God, but this is
the film that made him a household name in

00:10:27.519 --> 00:10:28.519
Brazil.

00:10:28.519 --> 00:10:32.029
The movie just oozes style, and it's absolutely
worth a watch.

00:10:32.029 --> 00:10:33.499
Thanks for watching!

00:10:33.499 --> 00:10:36.019
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:10:36.019 --> 00:10:38.170
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

